WEBVTT

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:23.620
--Enjoy.
--Well, during this time of year...

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:26.330
That goes out front.

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:28.120
Got it.

00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:30.380
Thank you.

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:33.090
Morning.

00:01:33.090 --> 00:01:36.420
It's also good for storing genomes.

00:01:55.070 --> 00:01:57.650
Please, take one!

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:42.240
How was the dive yesterday, Tsuneo?

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:44.370
I saw a <i>Priolepis nocturna</i>.

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:46.290
That's quite a find!

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:49.870
I was lucky the sea was so calm yesterday.

00:02:50.710 --> 00:02:54.290
You're on summer break from college?

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:55.590
That's right.

00:02:55.590 --> 00:02:59.130
How about doing a dive next Wednesday?

00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:00.930
Sure!

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:02.930
Bring some girls, too.

00:03:02.930 --> 00:03:04.470
Sorry?

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:08.060
The fish will be our lovers at this rate.

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:11.270
I want a human one, though. Right, Tsuneo?

00:03:11.270 --> 00:03:17.360
I don't have time. I start another
part-time job next Wednesday.

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:20.200
You're wasting your youth.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:23.490
You only get one summer at age 22!

00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:24.820
Whatever.

00:03:24.820 --> 00:03:26.450
Tsuneo!

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:29.910
Thank you.

00:03:40.130 --> 00:03:42.550
If I'm remembering right,
it was this way...

00:03:42.550 --> 00:03:45.680
Ahhhhhhh!

00:04:08.950 --> 00:04:10.950
Ouch...

00:04:12.830 --> 00:04:15.710
A-Are you okay?

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:25.260
Kumiko!

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:28.470
Kumiko, are you all right?

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:38.270
Did you save her, young man? Thank you.

00:04:38.270 --> 00:04:39.650
You're welcome...

00:04:39.650 --> 00:04:41.480
Are you injured?

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:43.900
I think I'm fine.

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:48.620
I turn away for one second,
and someone pushes her.

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:51.540
I almost had a heart attack.

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:54.250
Ow! Why'd you do that?

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:56.370
--Pervert.
--What?

00:04:56.370 --> 00:05:00.300
Stop touching me, you pervert!

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:10.430
The pervert is following us, Grandma.

00:05:10.430 --> 00:05:12.850
My house is this way.

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:15.940
Shall I push?

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:17.350
No.

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:24.400
Born this way.

00:05:26.650 --> 00:05:29.160
What about our walk, Grandma?

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:32.990
We're going home. No walks for a while.

00:05:32.990 --> 00:05:34.540
I don't want that!

00:05:34.540 --> 00:05:39.130
Tough. You can't have everything your way.

00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:45.170
Do you always take walks at this hour?

00:05:45.170 --> 00:05:50.600
I thought it'd be safer
and we wouldn't be seen.

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:54.810
But the world is full of scary beasts.

00:05:55.770 --> 00:05:58.140
Here we are.

00:06:08.570 --> 00:06:10.620
Then I'll be going.

00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:12.990
Come on in.

00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:16.250
You haven't eaten, have you?

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:22.460
Oh, drat.

00:06:22.460 --> 00:06:27.470
Is <i>takoyaki </i>okay?
We don't have any rice.

00:06:27.470 --> 00:06:29.430
Ah, that's all right.

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:41.350
Again?

00:06:41.350 --> 00:06:43.980
I keep putting him out, but he returns.

00:06:43.980 --> 00:06:47.940
Don't touch him, Kumiko.
He may have fleas.

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:50.030
Scat!

00:06:50.030 --> 00:06:52.660
He's only here for some free food.

00:06:52.660 --> 00:06:55.410
Really? Do you feed him often?

00:06:55.410 --> 00:06:57.450
I was talking about you.

00:06:59.620 --> 00:07:03.790
He's not a friend, just a pervert.

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:05.340
He can understand you?

00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:08.840
Of course he can't. Are you stupid?

00:07:10.760 --> 00:07:13.470
"Hurry up and leave my territory."

00:07:13.470 --> 00:07:16.180
That's what he's saying.

00:07:16.180 --> 00:07:17.430
Hey, Kumiko...

00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:19.060
Josee.

00:07:20.060 --> 00:07:22.810
My name isn't Kumiko. It's Josee.

00:07:22.810 --> 00:07:24.770
Josee?

00:07:33.620 --> 00:07:35.330
Thank you for the meal.

00:07:41.870 --> 00:07:44.210
Have seconds.

00:07:44.210 --> 00:07:49.460
Thank you. I can't afford
to buy another box lunch.

00:07:49.460 --> 00:07:53.050
You must be very poor. Are you a student?

00:07:53.050 --> 00:07:56.510
Yes. I live alone in a nearby apartment.

00:07:56.510 --> 00:08:01.230
I'm poor, but I'm trying to save money.

00:08:01.230 --> 00:08:04.020
Nobody asked for that much information.

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:06.150
I'm thirsty, Grandma.

00:08:06.150 --> 00:08:08.150
Barley tea or water?

00:08:08.150 --> 00:08:10.320
--Barley tea.
--Coming right up.

00:08:10.320 --> 00:08:12.070
Just a second.

00:08:12.070 --> 00:08:13.910
Ah, allow me.

00:08:13.910 --> 00:08:18.080
It's okay. Don't let your food get cold.

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:20.040
This must be it.

00:08:22.210 --> 00:08:24.460
Here.

00:08:24.460 --> 00:08:26.330
You're pretty demanding.

00:08:26.330 --> 00:08:28.800
Ow, that's hot!

00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:34.510
What's her problem?

00:08:34.510 --> 00:08:38.930
Kumiko can't hold cups with tea inside.

00:08:38.930 --> 00:08:43.940
Can't she use a bottle or something, then?

00:08:43.940 --> 00:08:46.270
You're a funny young man.

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:49.570
The food was delicious.

00:08:49.570 --> 00:08:51.190
Sorry to stay so long.

00:08:51.190 --> 00:08:54.780
Nonsense. We don't often have guests.

00:08:54.780 --> 00:08:56.360
Goodbye.

00:08:58.370 --> 00:09:01.830
You said you were saving money, right?

00:09:02.950 --> 00:09:04.710
A new job?

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:10.130
Someone I met said they'd
introduce me. It pays real well.

00:09:10.130 --> 00:09:12.380
What about this job?

00:09:12.380 --> 00:09:14.630
I'll continue, of course.

00:09:15.510 --> 00:09:18.720
Where's the joy in working so much?

00:09:18.720 --> 00:09:22.600
The person who recommended me was female.
You want an introduction, Hayato?

00:09:22.600 --> 00:09:24.100
Seriously?!

00:09:24.100 --> 00:09:26.020
An elderly woman who's about 80.

00:09:26.020 --> 00:09:27.730
Seriously...

00:09:27.730 --> 00:09:30.110
Move those hands, Hayato.

00:09:30.110 --> 00:09:31.860
Yeah, yeah.

00:09:33.070 --> 00:09:35.400
Have you seen the toolbox?

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:39.740
The metal lid was broken, so I fixed it.

00:09:39.740 --> 00:09:41.330
Thanks!

00:09:42.830 --> 00:09:47.170
I'm glad you're so thoughtful.
It makes me want you here full-time.

00:09:47.170 --> 00:09:48.960
I'll think about it.

00:09:48.960 --> 00:09:52.380
Not you. I meant Tsuneo Suzukawa here.

00:09:52.380 --> 00:09:56.550
I plan to study abroad after college.

00:09:57.130 --> 00:10:01.640
Didn't you know, Boss?
He's going to the Netherlands next year.

00:10:01.640 --> 00:10:02.970
It's Mexico.

00:10:02.970 --> 00:10:08.560
Ah, Mexico. I once swam
with a baby sea lion in La Paz.

00:10:08.560 --> 00:10:13.020
So, you're studying abroad...
We're going to miss you.

00:10:13.020 --> 00:10:15.940
I haven't decided on which school, though.

00:10:15.940 --> 00:10:21.120
He hasn't saved enough, either.
You should raise his hourly pay.

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:22.740
While you're at it, raise mine, too!

00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:24.620
Are you done checking the machines?

00:10:24.620 --> 00:10:26.830
I'll get right on it!

00:10:27.620 --> 00:10:29.170
What's wrong, Mai?

00:10:29.170 --> 00:10:34.750
It's nothing... Why don't you tell me
about this part-time job that pays well?

00:10:34.750 --> 00:10:37.720
You're to follow Kumiko's orders.

00:10:38.300 --> 00:10:40.760
--What?
--Didn't I tell you?

00:10:40.760 --> 00:10:45.770
No, you didn't! So, basically...
I would be working here?

00:10:45.770 --> 00:10:48.310
You'd be working here.

00:10:50.560 --> 00:10:53.150
Don't look so sullen.

00:10:53.150 --> 00:10:58.450
As long as you don't go out with Kumiko
on your own, everything will be fine.

00:10:58.450 --> 00:11:03.620
Help yourself to anything in the fridge.
There's pre-made food in there, too.

00:11:03.620 --> 00:11:07.450
I'm leaving now. Go and ask Kumiko
if you have any other questions.

00:11:07.450 --> 00:11:10.250
Wait, where are you...?

00:11:20.380 --> 00:11:22.140
Hello.

00:11:23.010 --> 00:11:26.930
What should I do?

00:11:26.930 --> 00:11:29.020
--John, was it?
--It's Josee!

00:11:33.610 --> 00:11:36.020
--Josee?
--Stay away.

00:11:39.650 --> 00:11:43.280
He's telling intruders to leave.

00:11:43.280 --> 00:11:48.040
But I'm working here starting today.

00:11:48.040 --> 00:11:49.620
Kneel.

00:11:49.620 --> 00:11:52.370
On your knees.

00:11:52.370 --> 00:11:53.960
Okay, I'm kneeling.

00:11:58.420 --> 00:12:01.760
Do you wanna die?

00:12:01.760 --> 00:12:04.140
Why am I kneeling?

00:12:04.140 --> 00:12:07.640
Because I want to know how long
a human can endure doing it.

00:12:08.350 --> 00:12:10.730
Do your job well.

00:12:15.060 --> 00:12:17.360
I'm going to make her cry.

00:12:17.360 --> 00:12:21.650
You've really changed in the past month.

00:12:21.650 --> 00:12:24.610
Is working for this Josee that difficult?

00:12:24.610 --> 00:12:27.370
It's way beyond difficult.

00:12:27.370 --> 00:12:29.540
Count the lines in the tatami mat.

00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:34.420
I can't sleep without knowing the answer.

00:12:34.420 --> 00:12:38.210
5,208, 5,209, 5,210...

00:12:38.210 --> 00:12:41.460
...5,211, 5,212...

00:12:41.460 --> 00:12:44.430
Oh, what a waste.

00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:48.430
I lost 8,000 yen at pachinko.
I should've picked a different machine.

00:12:48.430 --> 00:12:51.730
8,001, 8,002, 8,003... Ah.

00:12:51.730 --> 00:12:53.940
Start counting again.

00:12:56.270 --> 00:12:58.820
Go and bring me four-leaf clovers.

00:13:00.070 --> 00:13:03.070
Four-leaf clovers, four-leaf clovers,
four-leaf clovers...

00:13:03.070 --> 00:13:06.030
Four-leaf clovers, four-leaf clovers...

00:13:06.820 --> 00:13:08.370
Here...

00:13:09.490 --> 00:13:11.450
Nothing's happening.

00:13:12.370 --> 00:13:17.130
It was a myth that collecting ten of
them will make your wish come true.

00:13:17.130 --> 00:13:21.380
--What wish?
--Don't speak to me. I'm busy.

00:13:24.470 --> 00:13:31.010
She looks meek, but then she speaks and
stings you! She's an Amakusa jellyfish!

00:13:31.010 --> 00:13:34.730
One of these days, I'll glue her
door shut so she can't leave!

00:13:34.730 --> 00:13:36.640
That's pretty underhanded!

00:13:36.640 --> 00:13:41.940
Wouldn't it be better if you quit? Don't
you need to write your graduation thesis?

00:13:41.940 --> 00:13:44.570
But I really need the money...

00:13:44.570 --> 00:13:47.910
You don't have to work at that house.

00:13:47.910 --> 00:13:51.830
You have less hours at the shop, Tsuneo.

00:13:51.830 --> 00:13:58.000
I understand that you want to make money,
but why not think about Mai...

00:13:58.000 --> 00:14:00.000
This is delicious, you know.

00:14:03.340 --> 00:14:05.590
Is Tsuneo here?

00:14:05.590 --> 00:14:07.090
Professor!

00:14:07.090 --> 00:14:10.930
There you are. Do you have some time?

00:14:12.060 --> 00:14:15.230
It's about your essay on Turing patterns.

00:14:15.230 --> 00:14:19.560
Do you remember how I sent it to a
professor at Mexico City University?

00:14:19.560 --> 00:14:23.570
It seems like he took a liking to it
and wants you to go study at the school.

00:14:23.570 --> 00:14:25.570
Thank you so much!

00:14:25.570 --> 00:14:28.910
That leaves the question of a scholarship.

00:14:28.910 --> 00:14:32.910
It'll be hard to pay with your finances.

00:14:32.910 --> 00:14:39.330
I'll study Spanish harder! I'll rewrite
my research plan and application form!

00:14:39.330 --> 00:14:44.800
Well, being eager is great and all, but
if you work too hard it'll go to waste.

00:14:44.800 --> 00:14:47.970
Don't push yourself too hard.

00:14:47.970 --> 00:14:49.180
Okay.

00:16:25.190 --> 00:16:27.730
I thought you were asleep.

00:16:28.900 --> 00:16:32.610
--Grandma, can't we start going walking--

00:16:32.610 --> 00:16:34.030
--No!
--Grandma, can't we start going walking--

00:16:34.030 --> 00:16:40.700
What if you get pushed again?
Can you protect yourself?

00:16:41.500 --> 00:16:43.540
Listen to me. The world...

00:16:43.540 --> 00:16:46.330
"...is full of scary beasts."

00:16:46.330 --> 00:16:49.300
Right? I know.

00:16:49.300 --> 00:16:52.470
Then stay home.

00:16:59.100 --> 00:17:03.770
How nice. You're free to go anywhere.

00:17:07.520 --> 00:17:10.650
Even if I wait, nothing will happen.

00:17:24.370 --> 00:17:26.080
Hello!

00:17:40.180 --> 00:17:44.890
I'll miss the money, but Hayato is right.

00:17:50.980 --> 00:17:54.030
Hey, I have to talk to you.

00:17:55.990 --> 00:17:58.910
I've decided to quit.

00:18:01.490 --> 00:18:03.040
Are you listening?

00:18:37.740 --> 00:18:40.070
Kumiko!

00:18:41.200 --> 00:18:43.740
Kumiko!

00:18:45.080 --> 00:18:46.540
What's wrong?

00:18:46.540 --> 00:18:49.500
Young man, Kumiko is missing!

00:19:04.060 --> 00:19:05.680
Wait!

00:19:06.470 --> 00:19:08.100
Where are you going?

00:19:08.100 --> 00:19:10.100
It's none of your business!

00:19:12.360 --> 00:19:14.570
Hey, let me go!

00:19:17.740 --> 00:19:20.160
You're leaving by yourself?

00:19:30.170 --> 00:19:31.290
--Why don't we call it a day...?

00:19:31.290 --> 00:19:33.080
--I want you to take me there.
--Why don't we call it a day...?

00:19:33.960 --> 00:19:36.460
I want you to take me to the sea.

00:19:36.460 --> 00:19:40.430
If you don't, I'll say you touched
my chest and make sure you're fired.

00:19:42.140 --> 00:19:45.760
Do what you want. Let's go back.

00:20:00.570 --> 00:20:02.990
This will cost you extra.

00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:12.580
It's 280 yen.

00:20:12.580 --> 00:20:16.460
It's for the ticket. I have a rail card.

00:20:16.460 --> 00:20:19.590
--Is something wrong?
--It's nothing.

00:20:20.970 --> 00:20:25.220
It's Tsuneo. I found Kumiko.

00:20:26.350 --> 00:20:28.310
E-Excuse me...

00:20:36.150 --> 00:20:41.280
I'll return with her as soon as I can.
Well... I'm very sorry!

00:20:45.490 --> 00:20:47.330
Tigers...

00:20:47.330 --> 00:20:48.660
There are tigers everywhere.

00:20:48.660 --> 00:20:50.200
Tigers?

00:20:53.580 --> 00:20:54.830
Hey.

00:20:54.830 --> 00:20:56.130
Hey, where are you going?

00:20:56.130 --> 00:20:57.380
Home.

00:20:57.380 --> 00:20:59.670
Huh? Didn't you want to go to the sea?

00:20:59.670 --> 00:21:01.380
You were so insistent.

00:21:02.760 --> 00:21:04.760
Hey, you bumped into her!

00:21:04.760 --> 00:21:08.050
What? She bumped into me.

00:21:10.390 --> 00:21:14.270
Are you serious? What a jerk.

00:21:14.270 --> 00:21:15.900
Hey, watch it!!

00:21:15.900 --> 00:21:21.940
--Shut up, granny!
--Mess with me and I'll rip out
your heart and feed it to you!

00:21:21.940 --> 00:21:23.490
I'm sorry!

00:21:31.620 --> 00:21:34.790
What do you want to do, Josee?

00:21:34.790 --> 00:21:37.290
Are we going or not?

00:21:47.300 --> 00:21:48.720
Be careful.

00:21:53.100 --> 00:21:54.270
Isn't it that way?

00:21:54.270 --> 00:21:56.020
No, it's this way.

00:21:56.020 --> 00:21:57.770
So, it's this way...

00:21:58.980 --> 00:22:01.190
Where's the elevator?

00:22:01.190 --> 00:22:03.230
Why are there so many people?

00:22:03.230 --> 00:22:05.240
Beats me.

00:22:13.370 --> 00:22:16.920
This isn't my first time on a train!

00:22:18.120 --> 00:22:20.710
Are you picking a fight?

00:22:20.710 --> 00:22:24.880
No. I was wondering how you saw the world.

00:22:25.970 --> 00:22:29.680
Forests, deserts, New York, Paris...

00:22:29.680 --> 00:22:33.010
I've never imagined them that way.

00:22:33.010 --> 00:22:34.850
I was surprised that you knew how to draw.

00:22:34.850 --> 00:22:37.520
You went in my room without permission?

00:22:37.520 --> 00:22:41.020
If that sea existed, it would be nice...

00:22:46.320 --> 00:22:49.160
You're pretty arrogant for a caretaker.

00:22:49.160 --> 00:22:50.370
Caretaker?

00:22:50.370 --> 00:22:53.790
Starting today, you're my caretaker.

00:22:53.790 --> 00:22:55.500
What's with that?

00:22:55.500 --> 00:23:01.080
--Look! An airplane!
--Really? Where? Where is it?

00:23:42.710 --> 00:23:45.130
It's like a dream...

00:23:54.050 --> 00:23:56.350
It won't be easy on sand.

00:23:58.560 --> 00:24:00.060
Are you okay?

00:24:01.100 --> 00:24:02.810
Don't push yourself too hard.

00:24:05.650 --> 00:24:07.400
Hey!

00:24:08.650 --> 00:24:10.860
I was given a quiz.

00:24:12.030 --> 00:24:18.540
My dad once asked me,
"How does the sea taste?"

00:24:19.540 --> 00:24:25.210
When I was a child, I had him
bring me to the sea once.

00:24:25.210 --> 00:24:29.130
But I was too scared
of the waves to go near it.

00:24:30.470 --> 00:24:35.600
He died without telling me the answer.

00:24:37.470 --> 00:24:44.230
I learned from books
that it's salty, but...

00:24:44.230 --> 00:24:47.610
This may be my last chance to find out!

00:24:58.080 --> 00:25:00.580
What are you doing?

00:25:00.580 --> 00:25:03.870
Put me down, you pervert! Stop!

00:25:03.870 --> 00:25:06.880
Don't you want to check for yourself?

00:25:17.100 --> 00:25:19.010
It's salty...

00:25:20.600 --> 00:25:22.640
It really is salty!

00:25:22.640 --> 00:25:25.020
Why is it so salty?

00:25:25.020 --> 00:25:26.940
I'm happy for you.

00:25:29.570 --> 00:25:31.030
Hey! Stop moving so much!

00:25:31.030 --> 00:25:34.150
It's salty! It's really salty!

00:25:44.660 --> 00:25:46.370
Hey!

00:25:51.000 --> 00:25:53.210
"No going out!" 

00:25:53.510 --> 00:25:57.090
Didn't I tell you to come back right away?

00:26:00.310 --> 00:26:02.680
If you do this again, I'll cut it off.

00:26:02.680 --> 00:26:04.350
I understand...

00:26:11.820 --> 00:26:14.070
Why did you come with me?

00:26:17.110 --> 00:26:21.030
I have a soft spot for people
who want to visit the sea.

00:26:22.410 --> 00:26:28.330
I love seeing schools of fish,
so I go diving often to see them swimming.

00:26:28.330 --> 00:26:31.540
I even work part-time at a diving shop.

00:26:31.540 --> 00:26:35.970
You know what a real sea looks like?
You've even swam with fish?

00:26:35.970 --> 00:26:38.090
Well, yeah.

00:26:38.090 --> 00:26:39.890
That's amazing...

00:26:42.470 --> 00:26:46.350
Do you have other places you want to go?

00:26:48.440 --> 00:26:52.610
Grandma takes a nap from one to three.

00:27:30.810 --> 00:27:33.650
Is this the first time
you've eaten a crêpe?

00:27:34.440 --> 00:27:38.570
No. I've eaten them with my boyfriends.

00:27:38.570 --> 00:27:42.910
I'm popular. I've dated five at once.

00:27:42.910 --> 00:27:44.780
Sure, sure.

00:27:53.920 --> 00:27:55.710
Here we go...

00:28:03.220 --> 00:28:04.680
Are you okay?

00:28:08.140 --> 00:28:11.020
I never knew there were so many blues!

00:28:12.730 --> 00:28:15.480
--Let's ride that!
--What? Hey, wait!

00:28:15.480 --> 00:28:16.940
Hurry up!

00:28:16.940 --> 00:28:20.490
This is amazing! Where's my house?

00:28:20.490 --> 00:28:24.070
Can we see Osaka Castle?
Hey, Caretaker!

00:28:27.160 --> 00:28:29.290
Afraid of heights?

00:28:44.340 --> 00:28:46.140
There we go.

00:28:46.140 --> 00:28:49.270
I'll make tonight's dinner, Grandma.

00:28:49.270 --> 00:28:50.980
You'll do what?

00:28:52.940 --> 00:28:55.520
Yukichi, come here.

00:28:55.520 --> 00:28:57.270
Yukichi?

00:28:57.270 --> 00:28:58.480
That's his name.

00:28:58.480 --> 00:29:00.240
You can't name him like that!

00:29:00.240 --> 00:29:02.780
Make this chair two millimeters higher.

00:29:10.160 --> 00:29:11.750
That was pretty good.

00:29:11.750 --> 00:29:13.500
Wasn't it?

00:29:20.920 --> 00:29:23.010
Stop that!

00:29:23.010 --> 00:29:25.010
Wait a minute!

00:29:31.180 --> 00:29:34.520
Stop that!

00:29:38.480 --> 00:29:40.980
We're in the sea...

00:29:40.980 --> 00:29:42.190
It's a seal!

00:29:42.190 --> 00:29:44.030
That's a California sea lion.

00:29:44.030 --> 00:29:45.360
It has horns!

00:29:45.360 --> 00:29:46.820
It's a <i>Naso unicornis</i>.

00:29:46.820 --> 00:29:48.450
There's a big one!

00:29:48.450 --> 00:29:50.040
Whale shark.

00:29:50.040 --> 00:29:51.450
What about the ones who became a group?

00:29:51.450 --> 00:29:53.080
Those are Japanese jack mackerels.

00:29:53.080 --> 00:29:58.960
One type sticks to reefs,
but the other swims the open seas.

00:29:58.960 --> 00:30:04.220
The latter form unique schools
at middle to low ocean depths.

00:30:04.220 --> 00:30:06.630
They differ in shape, color, and habitat.

00:30:06.630 --> 00:30:12.390
Gold and black mackerel stick to reefs.
Rockfish take to the open sea.

00:30:28.870 --> 00:30:31.660
It's a job opportunity for Kumiko.

00:30:31.660 --> 00:30:34.080
You're as pesky as the rest.

00:30:35.120 --> 00:30:38.250
--She must be able to live independently--

00:30:38.250 --> 00:30:42.130
-- "It's the consultant's job to support."
--She must be able to live independently--

00:30:42.130 --> 00:30:46.590
I'm sick and tired of hearing that.

00:30:46.590 --> 00:30:52.850
I've said this repeatedly, but keeping
her at home isn't in her best interests.

00:30:52.850 --> 00:30:57.140
I'm sure Kumiko's deceased
parents are worried as well.

00:30:57.140 --> 00:30:59.400
You don't understand anything!

00:31:00.900 --> 00:31:04.400
I won't take Kumiko outside.

00:31:06.490 --> 00:31:10.990
However, she's been going out a lot.

00:31:10.990 --> 00:31:13.790
She thinks she's slipping past me.

00:31:13.790 --> 00:31:15.540
She's going out by herself?

00:31:17.370 --> 00:31:23.420
I didn't think he would take
her outside. I was shocked.

00:31:23.420 --> 00:31:27.050
You'd be surprised if you saw her now.

00:31:27.050 --> 00:31:30.760
She looks like that Dotonbori Glico sign.

00:31:30.760 --> 00:31:32.260
I'm sorry?

00:31:34.100 --> 00:31:37.520
As if she's ready to take off running.

00:31:45.030 --> 00:31:47.030
It's a sea of books...

00:32:02.000 --> 00:32:03.380
Josee?

00:32:05.670 --> 00:32:07.960
Oh, it's you, Caretaker.

00:32:07.960 --> 00:32:10.260
Didn't that say "Josee"?

00:32:10.260 --> 00:32:13.640
The main character's name is Josee.

00:32:13.640 --> 00:32:16.390
Françoise Sagan...

00:32:17.310 --> 00:32:24.150
That's the sequel to this one,
the conclusion I've longed to read.

00:32:24.150 --> 00:32:27.730
Hmm. It sounds like it'll put me to sleep.

00:32:27.730 --> 00:32:32.740
I wouldn't expect an uncouth person
like you to understand Sagan's talent.

00:32:32.740 --> 00:32:34.700
Go and borrow these two books.

00:32:35.830 --> 00:32:37.790
We need to make a library card.

00:32:39.080 --> 00:32:41.330
"Lost Profile" 

00:32:42.710 --> 00:32:44.880
Is this your first time borrowing a book?

00:32:45.880 --> 00:32:48.760
Then, please fill out this form.

00:32:52.880 --> 00:32:55.180
Do you like Sagan?

00:33:01.980 --> 00:33:03.730
So do I!

00:33:03.730 --> 00:33:06.060
Which of her works is your favorite?

00:33:08.070 --> 00:33:13.820
I'm sorry. This is my first time meeting
another Sagan fan, so I'm pretty happy.

00:33:15.950 --> 00:33:19.410
<i>Those Without Shadows</i>.

00:33:19.410 --> 00:33:21.410
You have great taste.

00:33:21.410 --> 00:33:23.370
Have you read <i>The Unmade Bed</i>?

00:33:23.370 --> 00:33:25.130
--That and <i>Those Without Shadows </i>share...

00:33:25.130 --> 00:33:28.670
--Josee, I borrowed them both.
--That and <i>Those Without Shadows </i>share...

00:33:28.800 --> 00:33:30.460
Is this your boyfriend?

00:33:30.460 --> 00:33:33.970
He calls you Josee. How nice!

00:33:35.430 --> 00:33:39.430
No, you're wrong! He's not my boyfriend...

00:33:39.430 --> 00:33:43.560
She wouldn't waste her time on me.
After all, Josee is pretty popular.

00:33:43.560 --> 00:33:45.940
She even had five boyfriends at once.

00:33:45.940 --> 00:33:48.770
Shut up, fool! I'll beat you senseless!

00:33:51.530 --> 00:33:54.860
Enough about that. I want to read the
book you were talking about earlier, too.

00:33:54.860 --> 00:33:57.240
Ah, the one about Beatrice...

00:33:59.780 --> 00:34:01.950
Aren't you glad you made a friend?

00:34:01.950 --> 00:34:03.290
A friend?

00:34:03.290 --> 00:34:04.710
The librarian we just met.

00:34:04.710 --> 00:34:07.880
Kana and I are friends now?

00:34:07.880 --> 00:34:10.130
That's what it looked like to me.

00:34:16.340 --> 00:34:19.800
Kana and I are the same age.

00:34:19.800 --> 00:34:21.470
How old are you, Josee?

00:34:21.470 --> 00:34:22.560
Twenty-four.

00:34:22.560 --> 00:34:24.680
Huh, you're older than me?

00:34:24.680 --> 00:34:30.610
No, it's nothing. So, you and
Kana are the same age, huh?

00:34:30.610 --> 00:34:36.240
Kana's amazing. She talks to so
many different people every day.

00:34:36.240 --> 00:34:42.160
When you work, it becomes normal. I talk
to customers when I'm at the diving shop.

00:34:42.160 --> 00:34:43.500
Really?

00:34:46.750 --> 00:34:48.580
Hey, it's Tsuneo...

00:34:48.580 --> 00:34:49.960
Hey.

00:34:54.880 --> 00:34:57.510
You're Josee... right?

00:34:59.840 --> 00:35:02.720
It's a perfect strike...

00:35:02.720 --> 00:35:06.640
Hello. I'm Tsuneo's best friend,
Hayato Matsuura.

00:35:06.640 --> 00:35:10.400
Would you trade LINE IDs with me?

00:35:10.400 --> 00:35:12.070
Really...

00:35:12.070 --> 00:35:14.360
I don't have one.

00:35:16.990 --> 00:35:20.740
She's a fairy...
A fairy living in analogue!

00:35:20.740 --> 00:35:22.080
Knock it off.

00:35:22.080 --> 00:35:23.700
What do you want to do?

00:35:23.700 --> 00:35:25.910
Sorry, I'll see you later.

00:35:27.580 --> 00:35:29.710
Welcome! A party of three...

00:35:29.710 --> 00:35:33.710
You don't have to worry about him.

00:35:33.710 --> 00:35:36.880
Please take a seat, everyone.

00:35:41.390 --> 00:35:43.600
Huh, what happened?

00:35:43.600 --> 00:35:46.310
I was in the area,
so I decided to stop by.

00:35:46.310 --> 00:35:48.730
How can I help you today?

00:35:48.730 --> 00:35:51.900
Um, we want to get our diving licenses...

00:35:51.900 --> 00:35:53.520
I see.

00:35:53.520 --> 00:35:56.150
It's nice to meet you. I'm Mai Ninomiya.

00:35:56.150 --> 00:35:58.820
Tsuneo's told me so much about you.

00:36:00.950 --> 00:36:04.910
If there's anything I can do, just ask.

00:36:07.830 --> 00:36:11.330
Ah, I saw a clown frogfish yesterday!

00:36:11.330 --> 00:36:13.540
Really? Were you able to take a photo?

00:36:13.540 --> 00:36:18.010
Because of the swells,
I couldn't really...

00:36:18.010 --> 00:36:19.920
I'm leaving.

00:36:19.920 --> 00:36:21.760
But we just got here.

00:36:23.470 --> 00:36:25.010
Josee?

00:36:25.760 --> 00:36:27.020
Sorry.

00:36:29.730 --> 00:36:32.350
Did Josee leave already?

00:36:32.350 --> 00:36:37.860
She was a type we don't have around here.
Fair-skinned, elegant, cute, ephemeral--

00:36:37.860 --> 00:36:40.860
Please get back to work!

00:36:40.860 --> 00:36:43.700
--What's wrong?
--Shut up, you fool!

00:36:43.700 --> 00:36:47.240
You're the one who wanted to see my job.

00:36:50.250 --> 00:36:53.670
I shouldn't come to places like this.

00:36:53.670 --> 00:36:55.290
Places like this?

00:36:57.840 --> 00:37:00.260
I don't know why
you don't like it here, but...

00:37:00.260 --> 00:37:01.720
You wouldn't understand!

00:37:01.720 --> 00:37:03.720
Yeah, I don't!

00:37:18.230 --> 00:37:20.070
I don't need your help.

00:37:21.650 --> 00:37:23.700
But if you're alone...

00:37:27.450 --> 00:37:30.830
Tell the caretaker to not come anymore.

00:37:31.500 --> 00:37:33.080
What happened?

00:37:33.080 --> 00:37:35.130
Just tell him to not come anymore!

00:37:36.170 --> 00:37:38.210
I'll do just that, then.

00:37:43.800 --> 00:37:46.390
I'm a mess, Yukichi.

00:37:51.430 --> 00:37:54.140
I don't have to come anymore?

00:37:55.520 --> 00:37:57.110
I understand.

00:38:03.820 --> 00:38:06.820
No, I don't!

00:38:17.250 --> 00:38:19.710
Isn't it good? I'm real proud of it.

00:38:24.510 --> 00:38:26.470
Um, this here...

00:38:28.220 --> 00:38:30.220
Excuse me for a moment.

00:38:30.220 --> 00:38:31.680
What is it?

00:38:33.680 --> 00:38:38.100
I was given a scholarship to study abroad!

00:38:38.100 --> 00:38:41.570
That's great! When do you plan on leaving?

00:38:41.570 --> 00:38:43.570
Next March.

00:38:43.570 --> 00:38:46.200
School begins in September,

00:38:46.200 --> 00:38:49.990
but the professor wants me
to leave as soon as I graduate.

00:38:49.990 --> 00:38:55.370
I see... Then that means we'll only have
six more months left to work together.

00:38:59.960 --> 00:39:04.090
You've been coming here alone lately.
What happened to Tsuneo?

00:39:05.840 --> 00:39:08.680
Who cares about that good-for-nothing?

00:39:08.680 --> 00:39:10.510
Good-for-nothing?

00:39:10.510 --> 00:39:14.140
He's useless, takes up a lot of space...

00:39:14.140 --> 00:39:17.560
Eats way too much, and fawns over girls!

00:39:18.190 --> 00:39:20.110
What's so funny?

00:39:20.110 --> 00:39:23.570
You're way too easy to figure out, Josee.

00:39:23.570 --> 00:39:25.360
What are you talking about?

00:39:25.360 --> 00:39:26.990
Kana!

00:39:26.990 --> 00:39:28.570
Rio!

00:39:29.860 --> 00:39:31.120
Read this!

00:39:32.200 --> 00:39:33.410
What's wrong?

00:39:33.410 --> 00:39:38.160
I read books to children around this time.

00:39:38.160 --> 00:39:41.130
A staff member suddenly quit, though.

00:39:41.130 --> 00:39:42.750
Excuse me!

00:39:42.750 --> 00:39:44.250
I'll be there right away!

00:39:44.250 --> 00:39:46.880
I'm sorry about that.

00:39:52.010 --> 00:39:54.010
Read this, Miss!

00:39:58.020 --> 00:40:01.060
<i>The Little</i>... <i>Mermaid</i>.

00:40:01.060 --> 00:40:04.610
She's going to read to us!

00:40:07.650 --> 00:40:09.360
I don't think I can...

00:40:09.360 --> 00:40:10.740
Hurry up and read!

00:40:10.740 --> 00:40:11.950
--Hurry!
--We're waiting!

00:40:11.950 --> 00:40:13.490
--Read the book!
--What about the rest?

00:40:13.490 --> 00:40:15.700
--What's wrong?
--Keep reading!

00:40:19.580 --> 00:40:24.000
"At the bottom of a limpid
blue sea stood a pearl palace

00:40:24.000 --> 00:40:28.420
where six mermaid princesses lived.

00:40:28.420 --> 00:40:32.800
They loved listening to the king's tales
of the world above the sea.

00:40:32.800 --> 00:40:37.600
'When you all grow up, go to the surface
and see the flying birds, exotic plants,

00:40:37.600 --> 00:40:40.940
and the lights of the city, '
the king stated.

00:40:40.940 --> 00:40:46.780
The princesses waited with anticipation
for that day to come, until finally...

00:40:46.780 --> 00:40:51.570
'Farewell, prince.' The Little Mermaid
tossed away the knife she was given,

00:40:51.570 --> 00:40:54.780
plunged off the boat, and into the sea.

00:40:54.780 --> 00:40:58.580
Her body began to melt into sea foam..."

00:41:03.630 --> 00:41:07.170
I can't read stories very well.

00:41:07.170 --> 00:41:08.920
Hey!

00:41:08.920 --> 00:41:12.220
What did the princesses' castle look like?

00:41:25.360 --> 00:41:29.110
Look, it's the Mermaid Kingdom!

00:41:29.110 --> 00:41:33.280
It really is the Mermaid Kingdom.

00:41:33.280 --> 00:41:35.950
Josee, you're an illustrator?

00:41:35.950 --> 00:41:37.580
No way!

00:41:37.580 --> 00:41:43.620
Really? It's a shame that more people
aren't able to see such lovely pictures.

00:41:43.620 --> 00:41:49.170
What if you made an anthology?
You could even publish it online--

00:41:49.170 --> 00:41:50.960
I can't!

00:41:53.680 --> 00:41:55.180
Sorry...

00:42:01.100 --> 00:42:02.640
Good evening.

00:42:04.020 --> 00:42:07.690
Leave! Dimwits like you aren't allowed!

00:42:12.150 --> 00:42:14.030
What're you doing?

00:42:23.040 --> 00:42:26.330
It's made pretty well, right?

00:42:26.330 --> 00:42:28.750
Did you make this, Caretaker?

00:42:28.750 --> 00:42:31.300
Yes, this caretaker made it.

00:42:32.340 --> 00:42:35.220
No wonder it's so ugly.

00:42:37.800 --> 00:42:39.800
What kind of fish is it?

00:42:39.800 --> 00:42:42.350
A Clarion angelfish.

00:42:42.350 --> 00:42:45.890
It's a rare species only found in Mexico.

00:42:47.150 --> 00:42:52.190
When I was a kid,
my local fish store had one,

00:42:52.190 --> 00:42:54.940
and I fell in love with it.

00:42:54.940 --> 00:43:00.580
I'd visit every day after school and
stare at it for what felt like forever.

00:43:00.580 --> 00:43:06.120
When I learned it was a species
that swam in schools, my interest grew.

00:43:06.120 --> 00:43:10.630
I thought, "It must really want
to be with its family, too."

00:43:10.630 --> 00:43:12.090
What do you mean?

00:43:12.090 --> 00:43:15.420
My parents are divorced.

00:43:15.420 --> 00:43:20.510
My dad left home, and my mom
was always busy with work.

00:43:20.510 --> 00:43:26.060
I don't think that Clarion angelfish
was really all that sad, though.

00:43:26.060 --> 00:43:29.150
After all, you visited him every day.

00:43:31.310 --> 00:43:36.440
It's my dream to see a group of
Clarion angelfish schooling together.

00:43:36.440 --> 00:43:40.370
I've studied hard, tried to save money...

00:43:40.370 --> 00:43:46.080
Because they're hard to find, I wouldn't
be able to see them on a trip, either.

00:43:47.540 --> 00:43:49.370
That's a nice dream.

00:43:51.040 --> 00:43:53.380
I hope it comes true.

00:43:58.130 --> 00:44:00.510
Actually, next year...

00:44:01.430 --> 00:44:03.050
This is defective!

00:44:03.050 --> 00:44:04.850
That's odd.

00:44:07.560 --> 00:44:09.770
There, all fixed.

00:44:24.830 --> 00:44:27.160
Ow!

00:44:27.160 --> 00:44:29.410
Ow... Why'd you do that?

00:44:49.640 --> 00:44:51.390
Hello!

00:44:57.860 --> 00:44:59.690
Come on, let's go.

00:45:05.660 --> 00:45:07.330
Kumiko!

00:45:09.700 --> 00:45:13.330
Grandma, the world isn't all that scary.

00:45:51.450 --> 00:45:53.870
I'm scared I'm going to have nightmares...

00:45:53.870 --> 00:45:57.040
You're scared? Didn't you want to see it?

00:45:57.040 --> 00:46:02.010
I wanted to see the
scariest thing here... with you.

00:46:03.840 --> 00:46:07.180
I thought I could if you were with me.

00:46:07.180 --> 00:46:08.970
Me?

00:46:16.230 --> 00:46:18.020
To cling to.

00:46:19.940 --> 00:46:24.530
If I get scared, I can cling to you.

00:46:28.740 --> 00:46:30.790
Ow, ow, ow, ow...

00:46:34.580 --> 00:46:38.460
I read a book to children the other day.

00:46:38.460 --> 00:46:41.090
You did? What book did you read?

00:46:41.090 --> 00:46:42.300
<i>The Little Mermaid</i>.

00:46:42.300 --> 00:46:44.970
Wow, that's amazing.

00:46:46.340 --> 00:46:51.810
I wasn't able to read the story well.
I was nervous and couldn't look up...

00:46:52.890 --> 00:46:54.640
I was scared.

00:46:56.520 --> 00:47:01.360
But then I drew a picture,
and the children loved it...

00:47:03.360 --> 00:47:05.950
I want to draw more.

00:47:05.950 --> 00:47:07.280
More?

00:47:07.280 --> 00:47:11.200
As work. I want to make art my profession.

00:47:12.700 --> 00:47:17.120
I want to try harder, like you.

00:47:19.960 --> 00:47:22.590
Well, I love...

00:47:22.590 --> 00:47:25.630
...your drawings.

00:47:25.630 --> 00:47:28.390
You're pretty arrogant for a caretaker!

00:47:30.470 --> 00:47:34.430
Cherry blossoms fall
like rain during spring.

00:47:34.430 --> 00:47:37.730
My dad used to bring me here.

00:47:37.730 --> 00:47:40.400
It must be beautiful...

00:47:40.400 --> 00:47:44.980
If you want to see it, bring me next year.

00:47:46.900 --> 00:47:48.660
Caretaker?

00:47:50.200 --> 00:47:51.830
It's nothing.

00:48:24.270 --> 00:48:27.360
Did you hear about Ms. Yamamura?

00:48:27.360 --> 00:48:31.410
She's had a bad heart for some time.

00:48:31.410 --> 00:48:34.160
She was also quite old.

00:48:45.210 --> 00:48:47.420
The morticians left.

00:48:49.300 --> 00:48:55.100
If you need to talk, I'm here to talk
about what you want to do next.

00:48:57.520 --> 00:49:02.520
Grandma left me a small amount of money.

00:49:02.520 --> 00:49:05.770
I'll be okay for a while.

00:49:05.770 --> 00:49:07.320
I see.

00:49:08.230 --> 00:49:10.990
But I can't afford it.

00:49:12.490 --> 00:49:16.280
I can't afford to pay you anymore.

00:49:20.830 --> 00:49:22.500
Okay.

00:50:09.920 --> 00:50:12.380
"Out of air" 

00:50:38.780 --> 00:50:42.750
It's rare for you to lose
track of your air, Tsuneo.

00:50:42.750 --> 00:50:44.910
You seem distracted today.

00:50:44.910 --> 00:50:47.960
I know. You hit on a girl and got reject--

00:50:49.630 --> 00:50:53.470
Josee's grandmother died.

00:50:53.470 --> 00:50:57.260
She's all alone now.

00:50:57.260 --> 00:50:59.680
She must be going through a lot...

00:50:59.680 --> 00:51:02.140
That's worrisome...

00:51:03.890 --> 00:51:10.020
But Josee isn't a child. There's plenty
of welfare services and facilities.

00:51:14.360 --> 00:51:20.410
"Free yourself from life.
From that which others call life.

00:51:20.410 --> 00:51:26.160
Be free from emotion, from one's
strengths, one's own weaknesses.

00:51:26.160 --> 00:51:33.170
Be but one momentary breath,
one-millionth of a billion nebulas."

00:51:38.550 --> 00:51:42.100
Are you home, Ms. Kumiko? It's Mizushima.

00:51:46.020 --> 00:51:49.350
This is Mr. Fujita. He's a social worker.

00:51:49.350 --> 00:51:55.860
The resident's association chairman
got a call from one of your neighbors.

00:51:55.860 --> 00:52:02.030
They heard your grandmother passed
and felt you needed assistance.

00:52:02.030 --> 00:52:03.740
It's none of their business.

00:52:05.580 --> 00:52:09.420
How do you plan to live going forward?

00:52:10.580 --> 00:52:11.960
Art.

00:52:13.500 --> 00:52:16.460
I'm planning... on making art.

00:52:18.510 --> 00:52:24.260
So, you're going to become an artist? You?

00:52:24.260 --> 00:52:28.060
I think it's wonderful to have a dream.

00:52:28.060 --> 00:52:35.070
Yeah, but dreams are one thing, and
reality is another. You should know that.

00:52:35.070 --> 00:52:39.610
Stop being foolish and search for a job...

00:52:39.610 --> 00:52:43.530
Your grandmother's not here to spoil you.

00:52:43.700 --> 00:52:45.410
Mr. Fujita!

00:52:45.410 --> 00:52:51.620
Is there someone else who'll support you?

00:53:12.150 --> 00:53:13.860
Are you okay?

00:53:16.190 --> 00:53:19.190
Um... we met some time ago.

00:53:20.400 --> 00:53:22.280
What do you want?

00:53:22.280 --> 00:53:28.410
I remember Tsuneo told me that you
lived along the river near Ni-Chome.

00:53:28.410 --> 00:53:33.540
Instead of splitting up and searching,
shouldn't we ask Tsuneo for her address?

00:53:36.750 --> 00:53:38.460
What do you want?

00:53:43.800 --> 00:53:46.550
Please set Tsuneo free!

00:53:46.550 --> 00:53:48.970
Wait, we came to cheer her up!

00:53:48.970 --> 00:53:52.520
He's worked so hard for his dream!

00:53:52.520 --> 00:53:59.230
He's studying Spanish, working many jobs
to save money, planning to study abroad...

00:53:59.230 --> 00:54:00.780
Abroad?

00:54:00.780 --> 00:54:06.120
Tsuneo is going to Mexico next March.

00:54:06.120 --> 00:54:09.370
Didn't he tell you?

00:54:09.370 --> 00:54:12.460
Would you support his dream?

00:54:12.460 --> 00:54:13.420
--At this rate--

00:54:13.420 --> 00:54:16.000
--Why do I have to hear this from you?
--At this rate--

00:54:18.000 --> 00:54:20.590
What's your relationship to him?

00:54:32.060 --> 00:54:33.730
He only feels sympathy toward you.

00:54:34.690 --> 00:54:39.230
Tsuneo stays with you out of sympathy.

00:54:39.230 --> 00:54:41.610
What are you saying?

00:54:41.610 --> 00:54:43.150
Don't mind her!

00:54:44.240 --> 00:54:46.660
Hey, wait up!

00:54:48.240 --> 00:54:53.580
What types of cytoplasm?
That's right, cytoplasmic genomes.

00:54:53.580 --> 00:54:57.420
Consider them a place to store genomes.

00:55:04.050 --> 00:55:06.800
"The Little Mermaid" 

00:55:12.850 --> 00:55:14.430
Hello.

00:55:21.360 --> 00:55:25.110
Josee, I bought some <i>taiyaki</i>...

00:55:27.280 --> 00:55:28.950
Why did you come here?

00:55:31.700 --> 00:55:34.450
Josee?

00:55:34.450 --> 00:55:35.830
This room...

00:55:35.830 --> 00:55:42.500
I had a helper come and clean for me.
They're going to come here once a month.

00:55:42.500 --> 00:55:44.420
--What about your art?
--I threw it all away.

00:55:44.420 --> 00:55:46.340
What? Why?

00:55:46.340 --> 00:55:49.180
It has nothing to do with you.

00:55:49.180 --> 00:55:52.180
If you don't have anything to say, leave.

00:56:06.490 --> 00:56:08.320
I'll fix it right away.

00:56:17.160 --> 00:56:19.080
I want to go to the sea.

00:56:21.170 --> 00:56:24.340
This'll be your last job as my caretaker.

00:57:02.790 --> 00:57:04.790
Do you want to go up to the water's edge?

00:57:04.790 --> 00:57:06.460
Right here is fine.

00:57:07.760 --> 00:57:09.720
Should I go buy you
something warm to drink?

00:57:09.720 --> 00:57:10.930
No thanks.

00:57:22.480 --> 00:57:23.980
It's salty.

00:57:28.280 --> 00:57:30.200
Josee...

00:57:35.330 --> 00:57:39.750
I don't need money.
Don't call this my last job!

00:57:39.750 --> 00:57:41.160
Josee!

00:57:42.370 --> 00:57:43.920
I'm no longer Josee.

00:57:45.420 --> 00:57:49.170
I've decided to work at an office.

00:57:49.170 --> 00:57:52.470
Even so, why did you throw away your art?

00:57:52.470 --> 00:57:55.260
It was out of my reach!

00:57:55.260 --> 00:57:58.010
It's always been that way.

00:57:58.010 --> 00:58:04.230
The red balloon caught on the roof,
the cicada husk on the tree...

00:58:04.230 --> 00:58:11.110
Walking under an umbrella in the rain,
running up the steps of a shrine...

00:58:11.110 --> 00:58:12.650
All of it...

00:58:14.530 --> 00:58:17.990
I'm not reaching for anything any longer.

00:58:19.290 --> 00:58:25.630
Then why do you look so sad?

00:58:25.630 --> 00:58:27.880
Don't give up on what you love!

00:58:30.670 --> 00:58:32.970
You're leaving soon, aren't you?

00:58:39.220 --> 00:58:41.890
The able-bodied wouldn't understand.

00:59:16.010 --> 00:59:17.430
Josee!

00:59:21.890 --> 00:59:23.140
Josee...

00:59:42.660 --> 00:59:44.200
Caretaker...

00:59:45.370 --> 00:59:46.870
Caretaker...

00:59:48.750 --> 00:59:50.170
Caretaker!

00:59:50.920 --> 00:59:52.380
Caretaker!

00:59:54.880 --> 00:59:59.050
Tsuneo!

01:00:05.180 --> 01:00:07.640
Are you all right?

01:00:07.640 --> 01:00:10.400
Hello, there's been a traffic accident!

01:00:21.740 --> 01:00:23.280
Remove the scoop!

01:00:23.280 --> 01:00:28.420
--I'm beginning to cut away the clothes.
--Pulse 120. BP 70 over 40.
Saturation 94%.

01:00:28.420 --> 01:00:30.710
Maintain 10 liters of air.

01:00:30.710 --> 01:00:32.090
--Did you confirm the peripheral?
--Not yet.

01:00:32.090 --> 01:00:35.630
Confirmed, hurry! Eighteenth gauge, open!

01:00:35.630 --> 01:00:38.050
--Cross match. Don't forget the blood gas!
--Yes!

01:00:38.050 --> 01:00:40.220
X-ray standby!

01:00:40.220 --> 01:00:42.260
Airways clear and respiration steady.

01:00:42.260 --> 01:00:44.010
We're beginning the echocardiogram.

01:00:44.010 --> 01:00:46.810
First negative. It's not a pneumothorax.

01:00:46.810 --> 01:00:51.560
Mr. Suzukawa! Mr. Tsuneo
Suzukawa! Can you hear me?

01:00:51.560 --> 01:00:55.150
If you can, open your eyes, Mr. Suzukawa!

01:01:17.760 --> 01:01:19.760
Do you know where you are?

01:01:19.760 --> 01:01:21.010
Um...

01:01:21.010 --> 01:01:25.310
You were in a traffic accident
and admitted to the emergency room.

01:01:25.310 --> 01:01:27.520
I'll go and call the doctor.

01:01:29.390 --> 01:01:32.020
About the girl in the wheelchair...

01:01:32.020 --> 01:01:35.690
Ah, we asked her to go home for the day.

01:01:35.690 --> 01:01:39.490
She insisted on waiting until you woke up.

01:01:39.490 --> 01:01:41.530
Was she injured anywhere?

01:01:41.530 --> 01:01:42.990
She wasn't.

01:01:45.410 --> 01:01:47.580
How do you feel?

01:01:47.580 --> 01:01:50.210
I heard I was in an accident.

01:01:50.210 --> 01:01:55.420
You suffered a concussion,
but it's nothing to worry about.

01:01:55.420 --> 01:01:59.630
Your internal organs
are all right. However...

01:01:59.630 --> 01:02:03.970
Your right shinbone's broken at the ankle.

01:02:03.970 --> 01:02:06.300
You have an open fracture.

01:02:06.300 --> 01:02:11.770
Emergency surgery was done
to prevent infection at the wound.

01:02:11.770 --> 01:02:15.770
We fixed the fracture with
screws and a plate.

01:02:15.770 --> 01:02:21.320
It will take two months before
it can bear your full weight.

01:02:21.320 --> 01:02:23.240
Two months...

01:02:23.240 --> 01:02:24.820
One more thing.

01:02:24.820 --> 01:02:30.370
Surgery couldn't unite
the joint surfaces perfectly.

01:02:30.370 --> 01:02:33.710
There's risk of osteoarthritis.

01:02:33.710 --> 01:02:36.710
Osteoarthritis...

01:02:36.710 --> 01:02:41.380
You may have joint pain and stiffness

01:02:41.380 --> 01:02:45.590
and won't be able to walk
or run as you did before.

01:02:45.590 --> 01:02:52.770
The hairline fracture in your left arm
may make crutches hard to use for a while.

01:02:55.100 --> 01:02:57.060
Will I heal?

01:02:58.650 --> 01:03:01.740
It's hard to say at this stage.

01:03:16.000 --> 01:03:17.330
Josee...

01:03:18.080 --> 01:03:19.540
I'm sorry.

01:03:22.800 --> 01:03:24.760
It's not your fault.

01:03:26.630 --> 01:03:30.180
I seem to be in pretty bad shape...

01:03:30.180 --> 01:03:33.810
Even rehab might not fix everything.

01:03:35.810 --> 01:03:39.940
If it turns out I can't walk again, I...

01:03:47.450 --> 01:03:49.070
I'm going to sleep.

01:04:05.470 --> 01:04:07.180
Shut up!

01:04:21.110 --> 01:04:25.940
You don't need to come, Mom.
Doesn't your back still hurt?

01:04:25.940 --> 01:04:29.070
It's no big deal, I swear.

01:04:29.070 --> 01:04:34.660
I'll come visit after I leave. Yeah. Bye.

01:04:36.750 --> 01:04:38.790
Professor...

01:04:39.920 --> 01:04:42.340
How are you, Tsuneo?

01:04:42.340 --> 01:04:44.920
I apologize if I worried you.

01:04:47.840 --> 01:04:51.680
Listen, about you studying abroad...

01:04:51.680 --> 01:04:58.480
They'd like another student to come
next March if you can't make it.

01:04:58.480 --> 01:05:02.980
It's sad, but you'll get another chance.

01:05:02.980 --> 01:05:07.190
You should focus on getting well for now.

01:05:11.030 --> 01:05:13.870
That's not the problem.

01:05:13.870 --> 01:05:19.710
I may not be able to dive anymore...

01:05:19.710 --> 01:05:25.170
If I can't, going abroad
will be meaningless.

01:06:06.210 --> 01:06:13.130
So, rotate your ankle
and flex your toes as best you can.

01:06:13.130 --> 01:06:20.140
When the swelling goes down,
we can shift to your rehabilitation.

01:06:22.600 --> 01:06:25.150
Tsuneo.

01:06:25.150 --> 01:06:26.900
I bought you some flan.

01:06:28.270 --> 01:06:29.650
Thanks.

01:06:31.440 --> 01:06:34.360
You started your rehabilitation, right?

01:06:34.360 --> 01:06:35.990
Yeah.

01:06:35.990 --> 01:06:38.160
I'll put this in the fridge.

01:06:39.580 --> 01:06:45.960
My parents send me rice and
vegetables, so my fridge is packed.

01:06:45.960 --> 01:06:47.040
Recently, they even--

01:06:47.040 --> 01:06:48.880
"Spanish Grammar" 

01:06:55.050 --> 01:06:57.970
Why don't we get some fresh air?

01:07:09.980 --> 01:07:13.570
Feel free to say what's on your mind.

01:07:13.570 --> 01:07:15.910
I'm here to give you my support.

01:07:17.910 --> 01:07:22.910
It doesn't matter anymore.
Studying abroad, Mexico.

01:07:24.540 --> 01:07:29.420
I thought I was stronger than this.

01:07:29.420 --> 01:07:31.420
Please don't give up.

01:07:31.420 --> 01:07:32.630
You can work hard with rehab--

01:07:32.630 --> 01:07:36.220
Work hard? What if that doesn't matter?

01:07:37.840 --> 01:07:41.970
I didn't understand anything.

01:07:41.970 --> 01:07:46.640
How scary it is to reach
for something you want.

01:07:52.320 --> 01:07:56.910
I... I love you, Tsuneo!

01:07:56.910 --> 01:08:00.990
I knew you didn't want a girlfriend
because you're about to study abroad,

01:08:00.990 --> 01:08:04.660
but I couldn't give up...

01:08:04.660 --> 01:08:07.870
I can't help it...

01:08:07.870 --> 01:08:10.380
I'm hopelessly in love with you!

01:08:16.930 --> 01:08:18.930
How did it turn out this way?

01:08:20.300 --> 01:08:22.260
Mai, I...

01:08:22.260 --> 01:08:24.810
I already know.

01:08:24.810 --> 01:08:28.560
I don't need an apology or your gratitude.

01:08:28.560 --> 01:08:32.360
I hate women who cry in front of men.

01:08:35.320 --> 01:08:38.740
But...

01:08:38.740 --> 01:08:41.240
...I'm glad I was able to tell you.

01:08:49.250 --> 01:08:51.290
We should get back.

01:09:11.520 --> 01:09:14.610
I know you're there! Open the door!

01:09:18.990 --> 01:09:20.950
If you don't...

01:09:22.200 --> 01:09:23.700
Go away!

01:09:25.040 --> 01:09:26.870
Don't come back!

01:09:29.000 --> 01:09:32.250
Tsuneo's given up on studying abroad.

01:09:33.460 --> 01:09:36.210
So now I'm making him mine.

01:09:36.210 --> 01:09:41.090
I'll give him the love he needs, so he'll
forget about the sea and his dreams.

01:09:42.590 --> 01:09:46.930
I didn't want him to go to Mexico, anyway.

01:09:46.930 --> 01:09:50.480
I wanted him to forget his stupid dream.

01:09:50.480 --> 01:09:56.860
I wanted him to stay by my side...
I've always wanted that, forever.

01:09:56.860 --> 01:09:59.860
I know him so much better than you.

01:09:59.860 --> 01:10:05.160
About his love for talking about fish...
About how he's horrible at humming...

01:10:05.160 --> 01:10:08.370
About how he always uses rock first
when he plays in rock paper scissors...

01:10:08.370 --> 01:10:15.210
He loves flan, hates cucumbers,
splits chopsticks badly, has cold hands...

01:10:16.800 --> 01:10:23.640
I could name a hundred, even two hundred
more things than you. I know him better...

01:10:24.890 --> 01:10:28.470
Don't stay silent! Say something!

01:10:28.470 --> 01:10:30.980
My caretaker won't ever give up!

01:10:30.980 --> 01:10:35.940
He'll never forget about fish
or abandon his dream!

01:10:35.940 --> 01:10:38.110
After all, that's who he is!

01:10:38.110 --> 01:10:40.610
You know that, right?

01:10:41.990 --> 01:10:46.280
I can't name a hundred things, but...

01:10:47.450 --> 01:10:50.950
No one can beat my feelings toward him!

01:10:52.290 --> 01:10:55.790
If that's true, then do something!

01:11:09.970 --> 01:11:11.890
They're salty...

01:11:20.650 --> 01:11:23.570
You're pretty clumsy.

01:11:23.570 --> 01:11:26.070
I'm a good woman!

01:11:30.370 --> 01:11:32.870
Why don't we go out
for some Korean BBQ, then?

01:11:32.870 --> 01:11:34.120
You're paying, of course.

01:11:34.120 --> 01:11:35.540
What?

01:12:10.870 --> 01:12:12.490
Josee...

01:12:14.750 --> 01:12:16.750
I have a request.

01:12:27.510 --> 01:12:32.390
I think you should make each character
speak about their personal feelings more.

01:12:32.390 --> 01:12:34.770
Let them say things such as, "How nice!"

01:12:34.770 --> 01:12:36.180
I got it.

01:13:13.010 --> 01:13:15.060
Hey, Brunet.

01:13:15.060 --> 01:13:16.600
Josee?

01:13:17.770 --> 01:13:19.890
Lend me your face.

01:13:19.890 --> 01:13:21.100
Huh?

01:13:21.100 --> 01:13:24.440
"Lost Profile" 

01:13:25.400 --> 01:13:30.490
"I desired nothing
but my escape from him.

01:13:30.490 --> 01:13:33.200
That is all.

01:13:33.200 --> 01:13:38.040
Upon reflection, it was a pitiful story."

01:13:45.710 --> 01:13:47.050
It's done.

01:13:47.050 --> 01:13:48.720
Ta-da!

01:13:51.760 --> 01:13:53.050
What's this?

01:13:53.050 --> 01:13:56.640
Can't you tell? An approval to leave slip.

01:13:56.640 --> 01:13:58.770
I'm not asking about that.
Who told you to file one?

01:13:58.770 --> 01:14:04.440
I figured you might've needed a breather.

01:14:06.190 --> 01:14:09.150
Sorry, but I'm not in the mood.

01:14:09.150 --> 01:14:13.410
Don't be such a bore, Tsuneo.
Let's go and have some fun!

01:14:13.410 --> 01:14:15.200
Stop bothering me!

01:14:20.790 --> 01:14:24.960
When you run out of air,
it's my role to help you.

01:14:26.800 --> 01:14:31.630
I'll help you breathe,
so just shut up and follow me.

01:14:37.720 --> 01:14:39.180
What's happening?

01:14:39.180 --> 01:14:40.930
Just listen.

01:14:45.230 --> 01:14:46.900
This is...!

01:15:10.010 --> 01:15:14.590
<i>T-The Mermaid and the Radiant Wings</i>.

01:15:23.730 --> 01:15:29.150
"From the floor of the deep blue sea,
festive music is heard.

01:15:29.150 --> 01:15:35.780
It's a mermaid's 20th birthday,
when she can leave the sea."

01:15:39.950 --> 01:15:41.660
You're doing fine.

01:15:48.040 --> 01:15:53.970
"The mermaid received
a magic shell as a gift.

01:15:53.970 --> 01:15:55.930
The magic shell then spoke.

01:15:55.930 --> 01:16:02.020
'You can use me to turn into a human,
and then back into a mermaid again.

01:16:02.020 --> 01:16:06.310
But you must not wish for anything else.

01:16:06.310 --> 01:16:13.860
For if you do,
you'll turn to sea foam and vanish.'

01:16:13.860 --> 01:16:18.990
'I understand, ' said the mermaid,
who proceeded to swim ashore.

01:16:18.990 --> 01:16:24.200
'O shell, turn me into a human.'

01:16:24.200 --> 01:16:28.540
Her fins then became graceful legs.

01:16:28.540 --> 01:16:33.550
'How nice!' the mermaid said
as she began to climb up a hill.

01:16:33.550 --> 01:16:38.220
But the outside world was full of danger.

01:16:38.220 --> 01:16:42.470
A ferocious tiger appeared before her."

01:16:43.100 --> 01:16:49.350
"The mermaid tried to run,
but she lost her footing and fell.

01:16:49.350 --> 01:16:55.360
Clinging to a rock, she yelled, 'Help!'

01:16:55.360 --> 01:17:02.990
Just then, a young man with pure white
wings descended from the sky to save her.

01:17:02.990 --> 01:17:06.120
'Thank you. Those are lovely wings.'

01:17:06.120 --> 01:17:10.540
The young man smiled
at the mermaid's words.

01:17:10.540 --> 01:17:14.920
'When spring comes, I'm taking flight.'

01:17:14.920 --> 01:17:17.720
The young man had a dream."

01:17:18.970 --> 01:17:24.430
"It was to fly to a shining sea far away.

01:17:24.430 --> 01:17:28.850
It was a sea where bright orange
fish swam together as a family.

01:17:28.850 --> 01:17:32.520
It was a sea full of fun and clamor.

01:17:32.520 --> 01:17:37.860
The young man and mermaid became
friends and went to many places together.

01:17:37.860 --> 01:17:44.370
'Every place makes my heart dance
with such joy! I feel like skipping!'

01:17:44.370 --> 01:17:48.910
The mermaid's worldview
grew with each experience.

01:17:48.910 --> 01:17:52.380
The seasons changed, and spring arrived.

01:17:52.380 --> 01:17:56.920
The day of the young man's
departure for the shining sea came.

01:17:56.920 --> 01:18:02.590
The mermaid was sad at being apart,
so she ventured into the woods alone.

01:18:02.590 --> 01:18:07.810
A ferocious tiger appeared before her.

01:18:07.810 --> 01:18:11.850
Claws sharp and fangs bared,
it pounced on the mermaid.

01:18:11.850 --> 01:18:18.030
'Look out!' cried the young man,
appearing just in time to save her.

01:18:18.030 --> 01:18:21.530
However, he was gravely injured.

01:18:21.530 --> 01:18:25.780
His gorgeous wings were also broken.

01:18:25.780 --> 01:18:29.500
Sobbing at the sleeping young man,

01:18:29.500 --> 01:18:32.960
the mermaid picked up the magic shell.

01:18:32.960 --> 01:18:36.250
'Please save him.'"

01:18:37.500 --> 01:18:43.590
"Within seconds, his wounds healed
and the young man awakened.

01:18:43.590 --> 01:18:48.010
However, the young man's wings would
never return to how they were before.

01:18:48.010 --> 01:18:54.310
'I can no longer reach the shining sea, '
he lamented to the mermaid.

01:18:54.310 --> 01:18:56.860
'Please, raise your head.

01:18:56.860 --> 01:19:01.950
After all... you have
larger wings in your heart.

01:19:01.950 --> 01:19:05.320
You guided me with those wings

01:19:05.320 --> 01:19:08.790
and used them to push me forward.

01:19:08.790 --> 01:19:14.460
With wings of the heart,
you can fly anywhere.'

01:19:14.460 --> 01:19:19.250
The young man set off for
the shining sea by boat.

01:19:19.250 --> 01:19:24.800
No matter rain or stormy winds,
the young man continued to push ahead.

01:19:24.800 --> 01:19:29.760
'I'm not afraid! I'm going
to make my dream come true!'

01:19:29.760 --> 01:19:35.560
The wings in his heart were
strong, supple, beautiful...

01:19:35.560 --> 01:19:38.570
...and most of all, unbreakable.

01:19:38.570 --> 01:19:42.280
'I found it. It's the shining sea!'

01:19:42.280 --> 01:19:45.280
The young man dived in with delight

01:19:45.280 --> 01:19:50.580
and began swimming together
merrily with the orange fish.

01:19:50.580 --> 01:19:55.170
'I'm glad his wish was able to come true.

01:19:55.170 --> 01:20:00.960
O shell, please turn me to sea foam now.'

01:20:00.960 --> 01:20:04.590
However, her legs just returned to fins,

01:20:04.590 --> 01:20:08.680
and nothing else in particular occurred.

01:20:08.680 --> 01:20:11.310
The magic shell then spoke.

01:20:11.310 --> 01:20:17.980
'Wishing for another's benefit and
not your own will never make you vanish.'"

01:20:20.480 --> 01:20:25.150
"So with a heart filled
with memories like shining jewels,

01:20:25.150 --> 01:20:29.990
the mermaid returned to
the seabed of the deep blue sea.

01:20:29.990 --> 01:20:31.910
The End."

01:22:18.810 --> 01:22:20.810
Why are you hiding?

01:22:27.980 --> 01:22:30.110
He might be able to make it!

01:22:45.840 --> 01:22:48.340
All right!

01:22:59.640 --> 01:23:02.810
Yukichi, my caretaker walked today.

01:23:05.860 --> 01:23:08.900
Stray cats shouldn't be so spoiled.

01:23:16.030 --> 01:23:18.240
I shouldn't get spoiled.

01:23:19.950 --> 01:23:21.960
I need to fight the tiger alone.

01:23:25.830 --> 01:23:27.710
The date for my hospital
discharge has been decided.

01:23:28.630 --> 01:23:32.470
As long as I make weekly visits
for treatment, I'll be all right.

01:23:32.470 --> 01:23:36.720
Really... That's great.

01:23:37.600 --> 01:23:39.100
Thanks.

01:23:41.060 --> 01:23:44.640
I'm not sure about the aftereffects...

01:23:44.640 --> 01:23:49.520
But I'm going to Mexico, no matter what.

01:23:49.520 --> 01:23:52.400
I have wings of the heart now, too.

01:23:56.160 --> 01:23:58.280
It'll turn out well.

01:24:01.290 --> 01:24:05.460
So, the date for my discharge
will be on the 24th. Well, about that...

01:24:05.460 --> 01:24:08.340
Will you come and meet me?

01:24:08.340 --> 01:24:10.090
At 10 in the morning.

01:24:14.260 --> 01:24:15.760
Josee?

01:24:18.050 --> 01:24:22.100
I'm just so happy.

01:24:22.100 --> 01:24:23.640
Thank you.

01:25:48.140 --> 01:25:49.890
Josee?

01:26:04.530 --> 01:26:06.080
Josee!

01:26:28.350 --> 01:26:29.930
Josee...

01:26:30.850 --> 01:26:32.350
Here.

01:26:36.900 --> 01:26:38.190
Kana!

01:26:38.190 --> 01:26:41.820
Tsuneo, congratulations
on getting discharged!

01:26:41.820 --> 01:26:44.910
--Where's Josee?
--I haven't seen her today.

01:26:46.660 --> 01:26:48.200
I'm sorry.

01:26:49.000 --> 01:26:50.960
You're right about that.

01:26:52.250 --> 01:26:54.880
Big trouble! Josee's missing!

01:27:21.990 --> 01:27:25.410
If you're looking for a woman in a
wheelchair, she boarded a minute ago.

01:27:26.780 --> 01:27:29.450
Do you know where she got off?

01:28:25.470 --> 01:28:32.430
Attention, guests. The zoo
will be closing in a few minutes.

01:28:32.430 --> 01:28:38.650
Please ensure you have all
your belongings and prepare to go home.

01:29:37.460 --> 01:29:38.960
Josee.

01:29:55.020 --> 01:29:57.980
Stop!

01:29:57.980 --> 01:29:59.520
I'm sorry!

01:30:17.040 --> 01:30:18.830
Josee!

01:30:31.840 --> 01:30:33.850
Ouch...

01:30:35.720 --> 01:30:39.180
You all right, Josee?

01:30:39.180 --> 01:30:41.640
What about you?

01:30:44.940 --> 01:30:46.690
Your leg...

01:30:46.690 --> 01:30:48.780
You just got discharged...

01:30:49.990 --> 01:30:55.200
In my panic to find you,
I found myself running.

01:30:55.200 --> 01:30:56.410
Why...

01:31:01.410 --> 01:31:07.000
I decided to become
a picture book illustrator.

01:31:07.000 --> 01:31:09.800
I plan to stand on my own two feet.

01:31:11.130 --> 01:31:15.640
You've pushed me
forward long enough, so...

01:31:15.640 --> 01:31:17.970
I'm not doing this for you.

01:31:19.270 --> 01:31:22.270
I wasn't doing this for you...

01:31:22.270 --> 01:31:24.350
I want to stay as your caretaker.

01:31:27.610 --> 01:31:30.070
What about the Clarion angelfish?

01:31:30.070 --> 01:31:32.570
When your leg heals,
you're going to Mexico.

01:31:32.570 --> 01:31:36.070
I'll leave, but...

01:31:36.070 --> 01:31:37.660
I love you, Josee!

01:31:46.250 --> 01:31:47.880
I...

01:31:49.170 --> 01:31:50.760
I...

01:31:53.630 --> 01:31:55.840
I love you too, Caretaker!

01:32:23.290 --> 01:32:26.080
It's not at all like I imagined.

01:32:26.960 --> 01:32:29.920
Um... Do you mean that in a bad way?

01:32:31.880 --> 01:32:33.630
I meant that in a good way.

01:32:46.940 --> 01:32:53.110
<i>So young and drowning in nostalgia,</i>

01:32:53.110 --> 01:32:59.070
<i>we were just looking at the sun
through a break in the clouds</i>

01:32:59.070 --> 01:33:04.790
<i>Going through the motions,
the voices flowing from us</i>

01:33:04.790 --> 01:33:12.250
<i>couldn't say what really mattered</i>

01:33:23.060 --> 01:33:28.810
<i>I tried to embrace a color without a shape</i>

01:33:28.810 --> 01:33:34.690
<i>Through the taste of regret, I've come
to know the days of hope and uncertainty</i>

01:33:34.690 --> 01:33:40.410
<i>I want to reach out to an unknown world</i>

01:33:40.410 --> 01:33:46.330
<i>I pocketed the lies
that made me sound tough</i>

01:33:46.330 --> 01:33:52.090
<i>The kindness wrapped in pain</i>

01:33:52.090 --> 01:33:57.470
<i>I want to remember it all</i>

01:33:57.470 --> 01:34:02.930
<i>If I just wish and wish and am born again,</i>

01:34:02.930 --> 01:34:09.390
<i>I'd still like to touch and sing
the glory of an uncertain future</i>

01:34:09.390 --> 01:34:14.520
<i>The taste of the tears
running down my cheeks</i>

01:34:14.520 --> 01:34:20.950
<i>reminds me of the promise we made one day</i>

01:34:20.950 --> 01:34:26.160
<i>It'll just turn to ashes and become hazy</i>

01:34:26.160 --> 01:34:33.340
<i>It'll go some place far beyond this night
and get absorbed into the blue</i>

01:34:44.390 --> 01:34:49.930
<i>All night long,
I tried to figure out my dream,</i>

01:34:49.930 --> 01:34:55.940
<i>but while I failed, the moon shone over us</i>

01:34:55.940 --> 01:35:01.860
<i>The day broke before I could go to sleep,
and I couldn't let go of your hand,</i>

01:35:01.860 --> 01:35:07.620
<i>but even though I adore you,
I wound up pushing you away</i>

01:35:07.620 --> 01:35:13.380
<i>My gaze that day</i>

01:35:13.380 --> 01:35:18.800
<i>has now become completely hazy</i>

01:35:18.800 --> 01:35:23.510
<i>It just hurts so much that it's killing me</i>

01:35:23.510 --> 01:35:30.770
<i>The sky is filled with
a blue so deep that it's cold</i>

01:35:30.770 --> 01:35:35.810
<i>We huddle together trembling</i>

01:35:35.810 --> 01:35:42.200
<i>and cherish the subtle warmth
we feel from each other </i>

01:35:42.200 --> 01:35:47.530
<i>The blossoms await the breeze
so they can drift into an unseen world</i>

01:35:47.530 --> 01:35:55.170
<i>They'll go some place far beyond this
night and get absorbed into the blue</i>

01:35:57.670 --> 01:36:04.970
<i>The mistakes I've made
and the regrets that followed</i>

01:36:04.970 --> 01:36:09.430
<i>are irreplaceable</i>

01:36:26.990 --> 01:36:32.580
<i>If I just wish and wish and am born again,</i>

01:36:32.580 --> 01:36:39.090
<i>I'd still like to touch and sing
the glory of an uncertain future</i>

01:36:39.090 --> 01:36:44.050
<i>The taste of the tears
running down my cheeks</i>

01:36:44.050 --> 01:36:50.470
<i>reminds me of the promise we made one day</i>

01:36:50.470 --> 01:36:55.730
<i>It'll just turn to ashes and become hazy</i>

01:36:55.730 --> 01:37:03.440
<i>It'll go some place far beyond this night
and get absorbed into the blue</i>

01:37:24.260 --> 01:37:26.380
--Pretty, huh?
--Yeah.

01:37:30.470 --> 01:37:33.140
It really is cherry blossom rain.

01:37:38.600 --> 01:37:40.650
Did you die?

01:37:40.650 --> 01:37:43.650
--What?
--Are you a ghost?

01:37:43.650 --> 01:37:45.530
I'm home for spring break.

01:37:45.530 --> 01:37:47.530
You didn't tell me!

01:37:47.530 --> 01:37:49.780
I wanted to surprise you, Josee.

01:37:53.160 --> 01:37:55.410
You're pretty arrogant for a caretaker!
